[1.408046, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.50591, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n"]
[2.505945, "o", "  identity: mnid:0f363de5c7909b664b83fb552a14d66c376b49ada334399c782360d86ba0e0cb\r\n"]
[2.506061, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled, private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/5a616b1b836757e5d7b37516d9ba53791e1ffa964ac220bb31785edbad7bb9a8.key\r\n  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[2.50647, "o", "  Created AGENTS.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[2.506572, "o", "  Created .claude/rules/mnema-instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .github/instructions/mnema-instructions.instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .cursor/rules/mnema-instructions.mdc, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Each holds the mnema instructions an agent host reads at the start of a session: when to\r\n"]
[2.506662, "o", "  call the mnema tools, and what never goes in the record. `mnema instructions --remove`\r\n  takes them out.\r\n\r\n  mnema writes no other file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n"]
[2.506942, "o", "  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n  project in a file of its own (the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names), and\r\n  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n"]
[2.507009, "o", "    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[2.507064, "o", "\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n  Off until switched on: edit-first-write-gate, user-corrections.\r\n  Turn one on with `mnema switch on <name>`; `mnema switch` lists every channel.\r\n"]
[2.507143, "o", "  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[4.127305, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
